      },
      "title": "Settings first, imports second",
      "description": "**What it is:** the top of the agent's main file.\n\n**How it works:** it loads `backend/.env` (or `api/.env` as a fallback) **before** importing the chat package, then adds the backend folder to Python's import path.\n\n**Why it matters:** some modules read settings like `DATABASE_URL` the moment they're imported. Loading `.env` later would be too late.\n\n**Watch out:** the comments above handle Windows: UTF-8 output and a special event loop. Your code was clearly run on Windows at some point."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/chat_server.py",
      "line": 95,
