          "character": 25
        }
      },
      "title": "Startup and shutdown",
      "description": "**New idea — lifespan:** code before `yield` runs once when the server starts; code after it runs when the server stops.\n\n**How it works:** both times, it deletes the temporary files that track live streams and approvals.\n\n**Why it matters:** stale files from a crash don't confuse the next run.\n\n**Watch out:** this cleanup only makes sense because state lives in temp files on one machine (later in this tour)."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/chat_server.py",
