      },
      "title": "A broken endpoint",
      "description": "**What it is:** an admin endpoint meant to show all the agent's prompts.\n\n**How it works:** it imports `ROUTER_SYSTEM_PROMPT`, `SERVICE_INSTRUCTIONS` and `AGENT_ROLES` from the graph nodes.\n\n**Why it matters:** those names no longer exist. The prompts moved to LangSmith (tour 08), so calling this endpoint fails with an import error.\n\n**Watch out:** a good example of code drifting after a refactor. Know it, in case someone opens it."
    },
    {
      "title": "What you can do now",
      "description": "### What you can do now\n\n- Explain how a FastAPI endpoint returns a stream, and why `X-Accel-Buffering` matters.\n- Describe the two queues and the two background tasks, and why they share one output queue.\n- Explain how the agent checks your login without talking to Neon Auth.\n- Name the single-server parts (temp files, memory) and what breaks with more than one server.\n\n**Next:** *07 - The LangGraph graph*. The graph that `run_graph` actually runs."
    }
